\b Cognitive Recognition Framework - Detailed Project Documentation\b0\par
\par
\b Version\b0: 1.0\par
\b Date\b0: 2026-07-08\par
\b Workspace\b0: Cognitive Recognition framework\par
\par
\b 1) Executive Summary\b0\par
This project is a hospital-focused computer vision platform that combines object detection, temporal tracking, RGB-D depth reasoning, and rule-based anomaly detection. The system is not a single model script. It is an integrated framework with four connected capabilities:\par
1. Model training and class expansion (from 106 classes to 109 classes).\par
2. Multi-model inference (YOLO ensemble plus Grounding DINO fallback).\par
3. Temporal identity persistence (ByteTrack) and scene-memory style logging.\par
4. Safety analytics (blocked exits, door keep-clear validation, spillage and 3D plausibility filtering).\par
\par
At runtime, the framework can process static images, videos, RGB-D sequences, and ROS bag style streams. It stores analytical outputs as annotated media, CSV and Excel logs, and SQLite spatial memory records.\par
\par
\b 2) Project Intent and Scope\b0\par
The framework is designed for hospital safety and operational awareness use cases:\par
- Detect infrastructure, clinical objects, PPE, and hazards.\par
- Track objects over time, not only frame-by-frame.\par
- Use depth to reject implausible detections and support spatial reasoning.\par
- Trigger anomaly logic such as blocked exits and obstruction zones.\par
\par
Primary design philosophy:\par
- Keep strong YOLO throughput for common classes.\par
- Add DINO only where YOLO is weak or missing.\par
- Preserve stable IDs and short-term room memory to reduce flicker and alert churn.\par
- Validate detections with common-sense and physical constraints before acting.\par
\par
\b 3) Top-Level Architecture\b0\par
The repository is organized as a clean framework copy with clear domain folders:\par
- 01_codebase: executable logic (training, inference, RGB-D, anomaly detection, object filters).\par
- 02_datasets: source and curated datasets, testing sets, archival datasets.\par
- 03_models_and_weights: trained model artifacts and reusable weights.\par
- 04_outputs_runs_and_logs: generated outputs, logs, validation artifacts.\par
- 05_documents_and_presentations: explanatory and presentation collateral.\par
- 06_database: database initialization and ad-hoc query helpers.\par
- 07_environment_and_project_meta: setup and dependency files.\par
- 08_media_and_3d_assets: media/3D assets used by experiments.\par
- 09_misc and 10_Testing: utility runners and validation scripts.\par
\par
\b 4) Core Pipelines\b0\par
\b 4.1 Training Pipeline\b0\par
Training scripts in 01_codebase/01_training implement staged adaptation:\par
- train_hospital.py builds a 106-class detector (80 COCO + 26 hospital classes).\par
- train_hospital_v3.py expands to 109 classes by adding bag, exit_sign, spillage.\par
- train_merged.py and phase2_retry.py support additional training orchestration and retries.\par
\par
Key training strategy details:\par
- Two-phase freezing strategy is used repeatedly.\par
  Phase 1: stronger freeze, train head first for class adaptation.\par
  Phase 2: relax freeze to adapt neck/head at lower learning rate.\par
- Dataset remapping is explicit, deterministic, and class-aware.\par
- Oversampling is class-specific for rare targets (for example spillage and exit_sign in V3 expansion).\par
\par
Output artifacts from training:\par
- model weights in runs folders and model storage directories.\par
- YAML training descriptors for merged datasets and class names.\par
\par
\b 4.2 Data Preparation Pipeline\b0\par
Scripts in 01_codebase/03_data_preparation curate and normalize data:\par
- prepare_hospital_dataset.py filters sparse classes, remaps IDs, removes unusable images, oversamples minority classes, and emits corrected dataset.yaml.\par
- split_and_rename_dataset.py creates train/val split for new_dataset and writes hospital_v2_dataset metadata.\par
- download_new_dataset.py handles external fetch workflows.\par
\par
Data curation mechanics implemented in code:\par
- Minimum support thresholds per class for train and val splits.\par
- Label-level remapping after class pruning.\par
- Copy and duplicate strategy for controlled oversampling.\par
- Deterministic randomization via fixed seeds.\par
\par
\b 4.3 Standard Inference Pipeline\b0\par
Scripts in 01_codebase/02_inference provide multiple runtime modes:\par
- infer_v3.py: V3-only interactive inference with Excel logging.\par
- infer_ensemble.py: V1 + V3 class-aware ensemble.\par
- infer_hospitalguard.py and infer_hospitalguard_v2.py: production-style layered inference with DINO fallback and expanded guardrails.\par
- infer_video.py and infer_hospital_image.py: media-specific wrappers.\par
- batch_test.py and batch_test_ensemble.py: batched evaluation and logging.\par
\par
Common inference logic across these scripts:\par
- YOLO confidence and IoU thresholds tuned around practical operation values.\par
- Class-routing policy:\par
  - overlap classes are merged through NMS across models.\par
  - V3-only new classes are sourced from V3 model outputs.\par
  - remaining classes come from baseline model routes.\par
- Structured result logging to Excel with TP, TP Low Conf, FN, FP, TN semantics.\par
\par
\b 4.4 DINO Fallback Strategy\b0\par
Grounding DINO is used selectively, not globally. The implementation emphasizes precision controls:\par
- Trigger only for weak classes or strategic classes where YOLO underperforms in domain shift.\par
- Isolated prompt mode for confusing classes.\par
- SAHI-style slicing for tiny object recovery.\par
- Context-anchor gating to suppress impossible scene hallucinations.\par
- Maximum box-area constraints to avoid scene-wide false boxes.\par
\par
Practical effect:\par
- Retains YOLO speed for most classes.\par
- Uses DINO as targeted recall recovery where needed.\par
- Reduces false positives through contextual and geometric guardrails.\par
\par
\b 4.5 Temporal Tracking Pipeline\b0\par
Temporal modules in 01_codebase/04_rgbd_and_spatial_twin/hospital_detector_temporal and longterm scripts add identity continuity:\par
- ByteTrack assigns stable IDs across frames.\par
- Lost-track buffer allows short occlusion recovery with same ID.\par
- Additional room-state memory caches recent detections to avoid alert flicker.\par
\par
Temporal alert extensions include:\par
- egress monitoring hold windows.\par
- exit blockage duration thresholds.\par
- geometric consistency checks between door and exit_sign.\par
- synthetic door fallback from exit_sign geometry when door detection drops.\par
\par
\b 4.6 RGB-D Spatial Twin Pipeline\b0\par
RGB-D logic exists both at top-level and in longterm development scripts:\par
- rgbd_spatial_twin.py replays TUM RGB-D sequences, syncs RGB and depth streams, renders side-by-side output, and optionally writes per-frame 3D points to SQLite.\par
- rgbd_hospitalguard_temporal.py fuses temporal object detection with depth-based localization and persistent storage.\par
- Additional scripts support OpenNI/Orbbec/RealSense variants and map visualization.\par
\par
Core RGB-D mechanics:\par
- Timestamp-nearest pairing between RGB and depth with max time tolerance.\par
- Camera intrinsics selection and depth back-projection to metric XYZ.\par
- DB insertions for object centroids and track metadata.\par
- Portable output video and logs under local output subfolders.\par
\par
\b 5) Anomaly Detection Subsystem\b0\par
The 01_codebase/06_anomaly_detection branch implements rule-centric safety analytics.\par
\par
\b 5.1 Blocked Exit Detection\b0\par
Main scripts include:\par
- Door-exit_Detect.py\par
- door_zone_rgbd.py\par
- Obstruction_detection.py\par
- RGBD_Reader.py\par
- SAM helper modules in sam_masker/\par
\par
Implemented workflow:\par
1. Detect and segment door region using YOLO + DINO + SAM.\par
2. Build 3D keep-clear geometry (half-cylinder zone) from door location and depth.\par
3. Detect non-door objects and refine masks.\par
4. Back-project object mask pixels to 3D.\par
5. Flag obstruction when object points intersect keep-clear zone over time.\par
\par
Important implementation traits:\par
- Cadence and hold logic aligns across door and obstruction stages.\par
- GPU assertion and strict model loading are used for predictable runtime.\par
- Output includes annotated videos and CSV logs for forensic review.\par
\par
\b 5.2 Spillage and Physical Plausibility\b0\par
Object-validation modules in 01_codebase/07_object_detection add post-detection sanity checks:\par
- common_sense_filter.py performs heuristic scene sanity filtering (for example impossible placement checks).\par
- rgbd_3d_filter.py applies depth-informed physical filtering using orientation-robust 3D dimensions and floor-plane gating.\par
- hospital_object_dimensions_approx.yaml provides class-level approximate physical ranges.\par
\par
The 3D filter uses:\par
- depth back-projection in detection ROIs.\par
- PCA-based oriented width/height estimation from point clouds.\par
- optional floor-plane estimation with RANSAC-like robust fitting.\par
- class aliases and dimension ranges for acceptance/rejection.\par
\par
This greatly improves trustworthiness for deployment-style decisions by rejecting detections that are visually plausible but physically impossible.\par
\par
\b 6) Data and Model Lineage\b0\par
\b 6.1 Class Evolution\b0\par
- Baseline training combines COCO classes with hospital-specific classes.\par
- V3 extension adds three additional classes: bag, exit_sign, spillage.\par
- Overlap classes across models are merged at inference with NMS.\par
\par
\b 6.2 Dataset Handling\b0\par
- Source datasets are curated through threshold-based filtering and remapping.\par
- Validation splits are deterministic where specified.\par
- Rare-class balancing is done through controlled duplication and selective oversampling.\par
\par
\b 6.3 Weights and Runtime Models\b0\par
- 03_models_and_weights stores stable train outputs and selected production weights.\par
- Inference scripts reference V1 and V3 model files by explicit path constants.\par
- Temporal and anomaly pipelines load additional models (DINO, SAM) as needed.\par
\par
\b 7) Database and Persistence\b0\par
\b 7.1 SQLite Spatial Memory\b0\par
Spatial memory table concept includes:\par
- timestamp\par
- class_name\par
- tracker_id\par
- X, Y, Z metric coordinates\par
\par
Database utilities:\par
- hospital_twin.db_init.py initializes required schema.\par
- query_db.py provides ad-hoc schema and recent-row inspection examples.\par
\par
In deeper temporal pipelines, additional metadata fields may exist in active databases depending on script version and evolution stage.\par
\par
\b 7.2 File-Based Logging\b0\par
The framework emits:\par
- Excel logs for detection QA and manual audit trails.\par
- CSV logs for per-frame temporal and spatial analytics.\par
- Annotated images and videos for visual verification and stakeholder communication.\par
\par
\b 8) Output Conventions\b0\par
Typical output locations include:\par
- 04_outputs_runs_and_logs for project-level generated artifacts.\par
- local outputs folders within specific code modules for workflow-contained exports.\par
\par
Generated artifacts commonly include:\par
- model checkpoints and run summaries.\par
- inference media overlays with class labels and confidence.\par
- temporal tracking videos with persistent IDs.\par
- anomaly clips and obstruction evidence.\par
- spatial map visualizations and trajectory exports.\par
\par
\b 9) Environment and Dependencies\b0\par
The project relies on Python-based CV and ML stack components, including:\par
- Ultralytics YOLO runtime and training stack.\par
- OpenCV, NumPy, and data handling libraries.\par
- Grounding DINO transformers stack for open-vocabulary fallback.\par
- SAM components for mask refinement in anomaly workflows.\par
- Supervision ByteTrack utilities for temporal tracking.\par
- SQLite and spreadsheet libraries for persistence and reporting.\par
\par
Environment folder contains:\par
- requirements files including specialized variants for hardware-specific execution paths (for example strict GPU + OpenNI).\par
- local virtual environment artifacts for reproducible runs.\par
\par
\b 10) Operational Flow by Use Case\b0\par
\b Use Case A: Train and Expand Classes\b0\par
1. Curate and filter datasets in data preparation scripts.\par
2. Generate merged dataset YAML with updated class mapping.\par
3. Run two-phase training for stable adaptation.\par
4. Store best weights in models and run folders.\par
\par
\b Use Case B: Standard Image or Video Detection\b0\par
1. Run YOLO inference (single or ensemble).\par
2. Trigger DINO fallback where configured.\par
3. Apply class-specific post-filters and context checks.\par
4. Save annotated outputs and structured Excel logs.\par
\par
\b Use Case C: Temporal Monitoring\b0\par
1. Run ensemble detections per frame.\par
2. Track with ByteTrack for persistent IDs.\par
3. Apply hold windows and memory stabilizers.\par
4. Emit temporal alerts and output videos/logs.\par
\par
\b Use Case D: RGB-D Spatial Safety\b0\par
1. Read synchronized RGB and depth streams.\par
2. Detect and track objects in RGB.\par
3. Back-project to 3D using intrinsics and depth.\par
4. Store spatial tracks in SQLite and generate visual maps.\par
5. Evaluate safety zones for obstruction and clearance logic.\par
\par
\b 11) Strengths and Engineering Decisions\b0\par
- Layered architecture balances speed and recall.\par
- Explicit per-class routing and thresholds are easy to inspect and tune.\par
- Temporal memory reduces unstable detections in real deployment scenes.\par
- Depth-aware filters materially improve physical credibility of detections.\par
- Logging and media outputs support debugging, audits, and stakeholder reporting.\par
\par
\b 12) Known Complexity and Risks\b0\par
- Multiple script generations coexist, so path constants can vary by script family.\par
- Mixed output roots can fragment artifacts unless run discipline is enforced.\par
- Hardware-specific branches (OpenNI, RealSense, strict GPU) require environment hygiene.\par
- Dataset and class mapping evolution demands careful version tracking to avoid label mismatch.\par
- Some ad-hoc utilities reference absolute local paths and may need normalization for portability.\par
\par
\b 13) Recommended Maintenance Practices\b0\par
1. Keep one canonical runtime path map for model and output locations.\par
2. Maintain a versioned class dictionary with migration notes.\par
3. Standardize logging schema across inference, temporal, and anomaly scripts.\par
4. Add automated validation for path existence, class alignment, and DB schema checks.\par
5. Document hardware-specific launch profiles as runnable presets.\par
\par
\b 14) Script-to-Responsibility Index\b0\par
\b Training\b0\par
- train_hospital.py: base merged-class training.\par
- train_hospital_v3.py: class expansion to 109 and oversampling strategy.\par
\par
\b Data Preparation\b0\par
- prepare_hospital_dataset.py: filtering, remapping, balancing, export.\par
- split_and_rename_dataset.py: train/val split and dataset rename pipeline.\par
\par
\b Inference\b0\par
- infer_v3.py: V3-only inference with Excel QA logging.\par
- infer_ensemble.py: V1 plus V3 merged inference.\par
- infer_hospitalguard.py and infer_hospitalguard_v2.py: layered YOLO plus DINO fallback with class-specific guardrails.\par
\par
\b Temporal and RGB-D\b0\par
- infer_hospitalguard_temporal.py: tracked temporal hospital monitoring.\par
- rgbd_spatial_twin.py: RGB-D replay and 3D point persistence.\par
- rgbd_hospitalguard_temporal.py: integrated temporal + RGB-D + DB workflow.\par
\par
\b Anomaly Detection\b0\par
- door_zone_rgbd.py: door-centered keep-clear zone in 3D.\par
- Obstruction_detection.py: object-zone intersection based blocked-exit logic.\par
- common_sense_filter.py and rgbd_3d_filter.py: plausibility and physical consistency filters.\par
\par
\b 15) Conclusion\b0\par
This project is a mature experimental-to-operational framework for hospital vision safety, not a single detector script. Its distinguishing value is the combination of model ensemble, open-vocabulary recovery, temporal persistence, depth-based physical validation, and anomaly-rule execution. The codebase is clearly moving toward robust real-world deployment, with strong emphasis on explainable outputs, safety-specific rules, and iterative tuning through logs and visual evidence.\par
\par
\b End of Document\b0\par
